.venv/
# media/ holds recordings (regenerable, large). The calibration YAMLs under
# media/calib/ are neither: they are the archival record of what the camera
# measured, and for the 2026-09-06 walk they are the ONLY record of it.
media/*
!media/calib/
media/calib/*
!media/calib/*.yaml
# The checkerboard docs/CAMERA_DAY.md tells the shooter to use. No generator exists.
!media/calib_board_9x6.png
# The 2026-09-06 demo renders. Committed deliberately despite the rule above: on
# demo day the video IS the deliverable, and a repo that documents a demo it does
# not contain is one clone away from being useless. ~144 MiB, plain git, NOT LFS --
# a teammate cloning without git-lfs would get pointer files instead of videos,
# which is a worse failure than a large repo. Regenerable from scripts/ plus the
# archived runs, but only while the container survives.
!media/phone_walk_slam_demo.mp4
!media/phone_walk_slam_demo_small.mp4
!media/phone_walk_map_3d.mp4
!media/kitti06_gt_demo.mp4
!media/kitti06_gt_demo_3x.mp4
!media/phone_walk_clip_selection.png
# NOT committed: media/map_building.mp4 is 100.7 MiB, over GitHub's 100 MiB hard
# per-file limit. It would need LFS. It stays on the USB backup and in media.tar.gz.
# media/nav2_goal_run.mp4 stays OUT of git by instruction, but it is RESTORED on
# disk (from Trash, 2026-09-06) because scripts/demo_day.sh needs it as the
# automatic fallback for the live Nav2 segment. demo_day.sh --check FAILs without
# it. If you clone this repo fresh, that segment has no fallback: pull the file
# from the USB media.tar.gz before demoing.

# The mission-control UI now lives in frontend/ instead of only in a Downloads
# zip. node_modules/ and dist/ are excluded by frontend/.gitignore, which shipped
# in the zip -- not repeated here. Sources are CRLF: do not let an LF-normalising
# editor touch them, or a 97-line change becomes a whole-file diff.
*.tar.gz
docker/build.log
__pycache__/
*.npz
phone_calib.yaml
vendor/
